@startuml
title R6's detector: what it can and cannot express\n(eight routes, each probed by execution)

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontSize 12

legend top
|= route tooling/runtime can take into an engine private |= detector |
| <b>from toolguard.config import _x</b> | <color:#137333><b>SEEN</b></color> |
| <b>from toolguard.config import _x as y</b> | <color:#137333><b>SEEN</b></color> |
| <b>from toolguard import config</b> ... <b>config._x</b> | <color:#B31412><b>BLIND</b></color> |
| <b>import toolguard.resolve as r</b> ... <b>r._x</b> | <color:#B31412><b>BLIND</b></color> |
| <b>getattr(compound, "_x")</b> | <color:#B31412><b>BLIND</b></color> |
| <b>from toolguard.permission_resolution import _x</b>  (post-D1a engine module) | <color:#B31412><b>BLIND</b></color> |
| <b>from toolguard.config_types import _x</b> | <color:#B31412><b>BLIND</b></color> |
| any private import in <b>hook.py</b> (runtime) -- <b>4 of the 5 real reaches</b> | <color:#B31412><b>BLIND</b></color>, pinned by a passing test |
end legend

note as N
  <b>find_private_imports</b> matches <b>ast.ImportFrom</b> only, on files whose
  first path segment is <b>tools</b> or <b>scripts</b>, against a hard-coded
  target set <b>{config, permissions, compound, resolve}</b>.

  The set predates D1a: <b>permission_resolution</b>, the module that now
  holds the decision machinery, is not guarded at all.

  Gaming move, DEMONSTRATED: the one reported violation imports a symbol
  that <b>config re-exports</b>. Re-pointing that single import line at its
  true owner (<b>rule_entry</b>, not in the guarded set) takes R6 to <b>PASS</b>
  with the encapsulation completely unchanged.
end note
@enduml
